        "title": "What Chooses a Representation Before the Seam?",
        "question": "How should Twilite choose Glyph, Icon, Summary, Detail, or full graph while the graph is still a node in workspace scope?",
        "status": "answered",
        "answer": "Use the graph frame’s rendered screen footprint relative to the available workspace viewport. Select only an eligible exposed authored View. Before the first authored threshold, fall back to a passive minimap of that graph and then its glyph at the smallest band. Full graph rendering begins at the upper seam.",
