    {
      "id": "semantic-zoom-view-selection-percentage-contract",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Percentage View Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": 740,
        "y": 700
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 390,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "key": "left",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## Optional View-owned contract\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"reading-view\",\n  \"type\": \"view\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"view\": { \"payload\": \"node.web.detail\" },\n    \"semanticZoom\": {\n      \"minPercent\": 35,\n      \"expandAtPercent\": 80\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`minPercent` changes when that exact View enters the sequence. `expandAtPercent` is meaningful on the highest-threshold View and changes when it yields to the full graph. Both are optional. Without them, exposed Glyph, Icon, Summary, and Detail roles use their conventional thresholds. Twilite sorts only the representations present in the graph, so missing roles are skipped rather than invented.\n\n### Generated fallback sequence\n\nWhen no authored View has reached its `minPercent`, Twilite renders a passive minimap from that graph’s visible nodes. Below 10%, it renders the graph glyph instead. These generated fallbacks require no declaration entry and never expose editor-only bridge plumbing in browse mode.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "semantic-zoom-view-selection"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
